<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seku Amadu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seku Amadu (Ahmadu Lobbo) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> Muslim scholar and reformer who launched a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massina">Massina</a> in the inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> delta in 1818 and founded the state known as the Massina <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> profile lists his movement among the West African jihads that were inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>'s example.</p></div>
